WEBVTT

00:00:03.225 --> 00:00:05.381
Open Queues and add a queue.

00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:08.741
On Routing, Routing strategy has three choices.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:13.750
Longest idle offers the call to the agent who has been available longest.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.252
Round robin offers it to the agent who finished work longest ago.

00:00:18.252 --> 00:00:23.451
Least busy offers it to the agent with the fewest active interactions, which

00:00:23.451 --> 00:00:27.445
matters little when agents take one voice call at a time.

00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:32.017
Prefer the last assigned agent turns on the sticky bonus.

00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:37.560
It applies to work that returns to the queue with its last owner still recorded.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:42.329
A new inbound call has no previous agent, so a returning customer is

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:44.521
not sent to the same person.

00:00:44.521 --> 00:00:49.097
Sticky never overrides skills, capacity or the order of declines.

00:00:49.553 --> 00:00:53.050
Reservation timeout is how long an offer rings.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:58.460
Unanswered offer action decides what happens when the agent does not answer:

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.693
Requeue, Send to voicemail, or Reject call.

